<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21292] unrm via setattr bypasses owner/CAP checks</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21292</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Found by code review of ex/lustre-release b_es7_0 @ 2.16.0-ddn63 (TCU, EX-428). Not yet reproduced on hardware; reproducer is sanity-tcu.sh test_10.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Problem&lt;br/&gt;
mdd_attr_set() (lustre/mdd/mdd_object.c:1326-1352) sets clear_unrm_fl=true for any setattr that clears LUSTRE_UNRM_FL on a trash object. mdd_fix_attr() then skips these checks when clear_unrm_fl is set:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;project-change permission (:708)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;flag-change owner / CAP_FOWNER (:757)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;chown CAP_CHOWN (:852)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;chgrp CAP_CHOWN (:883)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Nothing checks that the caller is root or the original owner (trusted.unrm urm_uid).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When trusted.unrm is absent (mdd.*.trash_can_{uid,gid,projid}=original, or a missing/damaged xattr; :1338-1340), the caller-supplied uid/gid are applied as-is. Any user who can reach a trash object can chown it to an arbitrary uid.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Reproducer&lt;br/&gt;
As root: mkdir d; chmod 1777 d&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;As user A: write d/f, then rm d/f&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;As user B: chattr -u d/.Trash/f or lfs trash unrm d/.Trash/f&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Expected: EPERM; the file stays in the trash with UNRM set.&lt;br/&gt;
Actual (by code): succeeds.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Suggested fix&lt;br/&gt;
In mdd_attr_set(), allow UNRM clearing only for root (CAP_SYS_ADMIN/CAP_FOWNER, RBAC) or when uc_fsuid == urm_uid. While clearing UNRM, ignore caller LA_UID/LA_GID/LA_PROJID and apply only the ids from the xattr. If the xattr is missing, allow root only.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Related: EX-14708, EX-13731.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
